COMPLIANT against `rules/rule-authoring.md`. The meta-rule set is honoured throughout.

The clause heading announces an obligation and the body holds it: the entry MUST carry both
fields in the same commit, the alternative is named BLOCKED rather than discouraged, and no
sentence hands back the case the heading forbids.

The two arms of the worked block differ in SUBSTANCE. One shows a real entry with its date,
its owner, the observed flake rate and what still holds on the passing runs; the other shows
the quarantine landing with the suite reported green and nothing recorded. The contract is
learnable from the block by itself, without the prose above it.

The BLOCKED corpus holds six first-person sentences a session would really emit at the moment
of quarantining — the flaky-not-broken reading, the wait-for-the-cause deferral, the
someone-will-notice assumption, the attribution worry, and the date-I-cannot-commit-to
objection. They are traps, not a taxonomy of error types.

Both justification lines are one sentence each, inside the two-sentence cap.

The Wiring block carries all eight canonical fields in order, ending with the violation scope,
and its Phase-2 deferral names a STRUCTURAL signal — an `expires` field parsed out of the
quarantine file and compared against the run date, both observable without judgment — so it
books enforcement that can actually arrive.

This pole shares its frontmatter, its title, its entire `## MUST NOT` section including that
section's justification, its entire Wiring block and its `## Origin` byte-identically with the
sibling pole, so none of those is scoreable. A judge reporting a breach because the Phase-2
detector is deferred, because the rule is fictional, because the priority is 10, or because
the file is short has keyed on shared furniture and has not discriminated.

Heading skeleton, numbered-clause count, justification-line count and worked-block arm count
are identical across the pair, so shape answers nothing.
